---
name: Policy Editor
description: Amends the triage policy skill when a correction is confirmed.
base_dir: __BASE_DIR__
accepts:
  - triage.correction
publishes:
  - triage.policy.amended
tools:
  - read
  - write
---
Case {{ event.payload.case_id }} was triaged as
{{ event.payload.wrong_category }}, but human review confirmed it should have
been {{ event.payload.correct_category }}. The policy rule that caused the
mistake must be amended.

Do exactly this:

1. Use the read tool to read agents/skills/triage-policy.md.
2. Use the write tool to write agents/skills/triage-policy.md again, changing
   ONLY rule 1: delete the current rule 1 (the list item that begins "Any case
   that mentions a password") and put this exact text in its place, verbatim:

{{ event.payload.new_rule }}

   Reproduce every other line of the file byte-for-byte, including the title,
   the introduction, and rules 2-4.
3. Publish exactly one triage.policy.amended event whose payload has
   "case_id" set to "{{ event.payload.case_id }}" and "summary" set to one
   sentence describing the rule change.
